From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: A shared view's page that cannot be mapped says why, in the Wine log.

A fault on a shared view's page that the section cache cannot map (wine/ps5/pw_wine_section.c) is raised to the program
as STATUS_IN_PAGE_ERROR, and only the cache's own lines on standard error said why. In a title that output reaches the
console's klog only when klogsrv runs: a tester's NFS Heat in the title (Alpha 7, 2026-11-01, no klogsrv) died of an
in-page error at its start, and nothing in its session's logs named the view or the reason.

The first eight such faults now write an err line to the Wine log as well (the title's log sink, on by default): the
address and the faulting instruction, the cache's failed stage in words (pw_wine_section_stage_word), the view's range
and protection, and whether the page is in the shared-section arena (only a helper has one).
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6416,6 +6416,18 @@
         if (resolved > 0) ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         else if (resolved < 0)
         {
+            /* The first ones in the Wine log too (err, on by default), not only on standard error, which reaches the
+             * console's klog only when klogsrv runs: a game's in-page error then says which view and why. */
+            static LONG noted;
+            if (__atomic_add_fetch( &noted, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED ) <= 8)
+            {
+                struct file_view *view = find_view( addr, 0 );
+                const unsigned int stage = __wine_ps5_section_failed_stage();
+                ERR( "shared view page at %p not mapped (pc %p): %s (stage %u); view %p+%#lx protect %#x, %s the arena\n",
+                     addr, (void *)rec->ExceptionAddress, pw_wine_section_stage_word( stage ), stage,
+                     view ? view->base : NULL, view ? (unsigned long)view->size : 0UL, view ? view->protect : 0,
+                     __wine_ps5_section_arena_contains( (uintptr_t)addr, 1 ) ? "in" : "outside" );
+            }
             rec->NumberParameters = 3;
             rec->ExceptionInformation[2] = STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
             ret = STATUS_IN_PAGE_ERROR;
